    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Intensity is the raw investment in a "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Power",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/power",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " — the amount of "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "CP",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/cp",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " poured into it at creation, or "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "XP",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/xp",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " spent on it during play (at 2 XP per Intensity point). It is the base that everything else builds on. Intensity determines the starting budget of "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Effect Ranks",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/effect-tag",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", the base "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Strain",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/strain",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " cost, and the ceiling of what the Power can do before "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Restriction Bonuses",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/restriction-bonus",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " expand it. A 1-Intensity Power is a precision tool. A 5-Intensity Power is a statement of commitment. Both are valid. Both cost something."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "What Intensity Determines",
        "id": "what-intensity-determines"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "Effect Rank budget:"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A Power's base Effect Ranks equal its Intensity. A 3-Intensity Power starts with 3 Effect Ranks before Restriction Bonuses are added."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "Strain cost:"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A Power's base Strain dice equal its Intensity, minus "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Restriction",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/restriction",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " discounts (minimum 1d6). Higher Intensity = more self-damage per use, unless offset by Restrictions."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "Total budget with Restrictions:"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Effect Ranks = Intensity + Restriction Bonus. A 1-Intensity Power with 4 Restrictions has 5 total Effect Ranks (1 + 4). A 5-Intensity Power with 0 Restrictions also has 5 Effect Ranks — but costs 5d6 Strain instead of 1d6."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Cost Scaling",
        "id": "cost-scaling"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "header": [
          "Source",
          "Cost per Intensity"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Character creation",
            "1 [[cp",
            "CP]] per Intensity"
          ],
          [
            "During play / [[spontaneous-evolution",
            "Spontaneous Evolution]]",
            "2 [[xp",
            "XP]] per Intensity"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The XP cost during play means mid-combat Power construction favors low-Intensity builds supplemented by Restrictions — which is exactly the "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "1 CP Nuke",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/creative-reciprocity",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " principle in action."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "You Died Variant",
        "id": "you-died-variant"
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "You Died sub-game:"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " In You Died, Intensity determines chip-cost budget for Power construction using the same formulas. XP-based mid-combat construction follows identical scaling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "See Also",
        "id": "see-also"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Power",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/power",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the ability Intensity defines"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "CP",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/cp",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the creation currency for purchasing Intensity"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "XP",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/xp",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the advancement currency for purchasing Intensity during play"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Effect Tag",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/effect-tag",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — what the Intensity budget is spent on"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Restriction Bonus",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/restriction-bonus",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — what expands the budget beyond Intensity"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Strain",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/strain",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the self-damage cost Intensity determines"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "emphasis",
            "text": "David Daniel, with Archive as scribe"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
