    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An Item is a piece of equipment with mechanical properties — a sword, a shield, a hacking rig, a courtroom badge — built using the item construction system and purchased with "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "IP (Item Points)",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/ip",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at character creation. Items have a Quality rating (Q1–Q4) that adds dice to the "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Dice Hand",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/dice-hand",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", a Durability Pool that tracks wear, and may carry tags and complications of their own. Using an Item in combat requires "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Employment",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/employment",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " — subtracting 1 die from the Dice Hand per Item employed. A character may equip a maximum of "
          },
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "3 Items"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Quality",
        "id": "quality"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "header": [
          "Quality",
          "Dice Added",
          "Net Gain (after Employment)"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Q1",
            "+1",
            "0"
          ],
          [
            "Q2",
            "+2",
            "+1"
          ],
          [
            "Q3",
            "+3",
            "+2"
          ],
          [
            "Q4",
            "+4",
            "+3"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A Q1 Item breaks even on dice — its value lies in its tags and narrative function. Higher Quality Items provide genuine mechanical advantage, but the "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Employment",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/employment",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " cost means every equipped Item still demands attention from the Dice Hand."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Acquisition",
        "id": "acquisition"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Items are purchased at character creation with "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "IP",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/ip",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", which is separated from "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "CP",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/cp",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to prevent dump-stacking all creation resources into combat "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Powers",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/power",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". After creation, Items can be acquired through gameplay, crafting, or "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "XP",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/xp",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " expenditure. The starting IP budget is "
          },
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "15 IP"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "You Died Variant",
        "id": "you-died-variant"
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "You Died sub-game:"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " In You Died, Items add bonus chips to the domain-specific chip pool, with the same Employment cost (1 chip per Item employed). Quality ratings and the 3-Item equip cap are unchanged."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "See Also",
        "id": "see-also"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Employment",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/employment",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the cost of using an Item in combat"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Dice Hand",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/dice-hand",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the resource Items add to (and Employment subtracts from)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "IP",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/ip",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the creation currency for purchasing Items"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "emphasis",
            "text": "David Daniel, with Archive as scribe"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
