    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A Skill is learned competence — the focused knowledge and practice that supplements raw "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Stat",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/stat",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " potential. Where the Stat is what your body, mind, or presence "
          },
          {
            "type": "emphasis",
            "text": "can"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " do in the broadest sense, a Skill is what you have trained it to do "
          },
          {
            "type": "emphasis",
            "text": "specifically"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Each rank of a relevant Skill adds +2 dice to the "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Dice Hand",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/dice-hand",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for actions that fall within its domain. A character with Physical 3 and Melee 2 rolls 3 base dice plus 4 Skill dice — 7 total before equipment. Skills are the difference between someone who is strong and someone who knows how to fight."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Skill Dice",
        "id": "skill-dice"
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "Skill contribution = Skill Rank × 2 dice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each Skill rank adds 2 dice to the Dice Hand when performing an action the Skill covers. Multiple Skills can apply to a single action, up to a cap of "
          },
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "4 Skills per action"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". A character with Melee 2 and Athletics 1 performing a leaping sword strike could apply both — 4 dice from Melee plus 2 from Athletics, for 6 Skill dice total."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Dice Hand is still subject to the "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Entropic Cap",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/entropic-cap",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". High Skill investment in a low-Pool domain gets capped — the Skills provide the dice, but the Pool sets the ceiling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Automatic Skills",
        "id": "automatic-skills"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "At character creation, each "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "Stat",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/stat",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " rank grants a number of Automatic Skills in that Stat's domain. These represent the baseline competencies that come naturally with higher capability — a character with Mental 4 knows more things than a character with Mental 1, regardless of what either has deliberately trained."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Additional Skills can be purchased with "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "CP",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/cp",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at creation or "
          },
          {
            "type": "wiki-link",
            "text": "XP",
            "href": "/wiki/glossary/xp",
            "status": "resolved"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " during play (2 XP per Skill rank)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Skills in Combat and Beyond",
        "id": "skills-in-combat-and-beyond"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Skills contribute dice to:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "text": "Combat actions"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — Melee adds to sword strikes, Firearms adds to gunshots, Rhetoric adds to verbal attacks."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "text": "[[scene-action|Scene Actions]]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — Athletics adds to chases, Investigation adds to searches, Medicine adds to field treatment."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "text": "Skill checks"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — Any non-combat roll where the Judge determines a Skill applies."
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The same Skill contributes the same +2 dice per rank regardless of context. There is no separate \"combat skill\" and \"exploration skill\" — if Melee applies, Melee contributes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "You Died Variant",
        "id": "you-died-variant"
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "text": "You Died sub-game:"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " In You Died, Skills add bonus chips to the domain-specific chip pool rather than dice to the Dice Hand. The per-rank bonus and 4-Skill cap per action apply identically."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "See Also",
        "id": "see-also"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Stat",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/stat",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the base that Skills build on"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Dice Hand",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/dice-hand",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the pool Skills contribute to"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Entropic Cap",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/entropic-cap",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the ceiling that limits Skill contribution"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "Scene Action",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/scene-action",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — non-Power actions where Skills apply"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "CP",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/cp",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — creation currency for purchasing Skills"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "wiki-link",
              "text": "XP",
              "href": "/wiki/glossary/xp",
              "status": "resolved"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — advancement currency for purchasing Skills during play"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "type": "emphasis",
            "text": "David Daniel, with Archive as scribe"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
